			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Synchronize submodule to latest maintenance revision\n\nUpdate the Maintain submodule from commit cb38969 to 4e4833d to incorporate the latest CI/CD configurations, GritQL queries, and maintenance scripts. This ensures the build pipeline and project hygiene tools remain aligned with the current ecosystem standards.\n\nNo changes to the core editor logic or dependencies; this update strictly affects the tooling layer responsible for repository maintenance and automated quality checks.",
			"SHA": "72c26dd79e1b4bbe4a4a644af37e901a888487dd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-16T21:44:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡿⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				10
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 10 submodules for performance optimization and IPC efficiency\n\nPerform a coordinated update across the Land Editor ecosystem to eliminate dead code, optimize IPC handling, and streamline build configurations.\n\n**Cocoon**: Enable production tree shaking and conditionally disable debug logging, reducing the Main.js bundle by ~10% (1.49MB → 1.33MB). Refactor the performance monitoring service to a zero-overhead shim, replace array reductions with O(1) Exponential Moving Average for latency tracking, and update bootstrap watchdog polling to 5s with `unref` intervals.\n\n**Mountain**: Enable full diagnostic tracing and implement robust TTY detection to skip shell enhancements in interactive terminals. Introduce a high-frequency command filter in `WindServiceHandlers` to bypass OTLP spans and Echo submission for silent commands (e.g., `logger:*`, `storage`), significantly reducing CPU overhead during boot.\n\n**Wind**: Consolidate Layer composition using `Layer.mergeAll` to reduce intermediate objects from O(n) to O(1). Streamline Tauri IPC argument serialization and standardize production builds to strip console statements.\n\nUpdates to **Common**, **Echo**, **Output**, **Rest**, **SideCar**, **Sky**, and **Worker** align with build hygiene and architectural consistency. These changes enhance runtime efficiency and prepare the stack for intensive testing.",
			"SHA": "a934a1ae06b9ed97941b0e9dee2e9c1430e71ce2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-16T01:09:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize Cocoon and Sky submodules for build refresh and IPC diagnostics\n\nPerform targeted updates to the extension host pipeline and UI component layer to ensure build consistency and enhance runtime observability.\n\n**Cocoon**: Regenerate all TypeScript compilation outputs in the `Target/` directory, updating the `RouteManifest` timestamp to the current build cycle. This synchronizes JavaScript bundles, source maps, and gRPC service definitions for the extension host sidecar.\n\n**Sky**: Instrument the `Bridge.ts` webview postMessage handler with diagnostic logging via `MountainIPCInvoke`. Capture lifecycle events including entry receipt, registry lookup state, dispatch attempts, and execution errors. Logs include ViewId and message metadata to facilitate debugging of IPC flows between the Astro UI and VS Code workbench webviews.\n\nThese changes ensure the extension host is ready for the upcoming testing phase while providing granular visibility into the UI-to-backend communication bridge without altering core dispatch logic.",
			"SHA": "5f2fcfab36919c346774cd8c194ad66019dfc706"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-16T00:37:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Regenerate build artifacts and update RouteManifest\n\nRebuild all TypeScript compilation outputs in the `Target/` directory following the latest source modifications. Update the `RouteManifest` timestamp to reflect the current build cycle, ensuring the extension host sidecar and gRPC services are synchronized with the latest source modifications.\n\nThis includes updated JavaScript bundles and source maps for bootstrap entry points, gRPC server services, VS Code API handlers, and the dual-track routing logic. All intermediate build cache files and generated manifest reports are synchronized to ensure the extension host is in a consistent state for the upcoming testing phase.",
			"SHA": "e5d00f5d13064ef7c079b442a3852b71da12fea1"
		}
